{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplication Property of Inequality.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplication Property of Inequality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multiplication property of inequality multiplication property of inequality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplication Property of Inequality.md","fileName":"Multiplication Property of Inequality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multiplication Property of Inequality","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Linear Inequalities and Intervals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Inequalities and Intervals","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplication Property of Inequality.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplication Property of Inequality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multiplication property of inequality multiplication property of inequality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multiplication Property of Inequality.md","fileName":"Multiplication Property of Inequality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multiplication Property of Inequality","heading":"Multiplication Property of Inequality","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The multiplication property of inequality depends on the sign of the common multiplier. If (a<b) and (c>0), then\n\n$$ac<bc.$$\n\nMultiplication by a positive value scales both positions without changing their order. If (c<0), the order reverses:\n\n$$ac>bc.$$\n\nDivision follows the same rule because it multiplies by a reciprocal. This sign-sensitive behavior is the key difference between solving inequalities and solving equations.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Inequalities and Intervals","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF3